WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.711
game day Jonathan couldn't wait to play.

2
00:00:17.432 --> 00:00:20.654
He got to the field early and helped his parents set up their chairs on the sideline.

3
00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:23.496
Then he tied his dog's leash to his mother's chair.

4
00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:28.080
A girl about Jonathan's age walked toward him.

5
00:00:31.148 --> 00:00:33.209
He'd seen her in school, but he'd never talked to her.

6
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.592
She was beautiful, with long, dark hair and blue eyes.

7
00:00:37.452 --> 00:00:40.434
She stopped right in front of Jonathan and said, "What a cutie!"

8
00:00:40.454 --> 00:00:43.336
"Whoa! She thinks I'm a cutie!"

9
00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:45.017
Jonathan thought, amazed.

10
00:00:45.037 --> 00:00:46.498
"Can I pet her?"

11
00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:47.699
the girl asked.

12
00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:52.082
"Oh. She thinks our dog is a cutie," Jonathan realized.

13
00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:53.983
Mrs. Cho smiled.

14
00:00:54.003 --> 00:00:55.724
"He loves being petted."

15
00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:58.486
The girl bent down to pet Pastrami.

16
00:00:58.506 --> 00:01:00.928
"Sorry for calling your dog a her."

17
00:01:02.568 --> 00:01:04.610
"No big beal," Jonathan said.

18
00:01:05.311 --> 00:01:05.851
He blushed.

19
00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:07.672
"I mean, no big deal."

20
00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:09.154
"What's his name?"

21
00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.214
the girl asked.

22
00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:12.937
"Strapami," Jonathan said.

23
00:01:12.957 --> 00:01:18.801
"Strapami?" "Pastrami," Jonathan corrected himself, blushing more.

24
00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:22.484
"Boys!" Coach Wattenbarger barked just then.

25
00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:25.186
"You'd better go to your coach, Johnnyboy," Mrs.

26
00:01:25.247 --> 00:01:25.747
Cho said.

27
00:01:26.668 --> 00:01:28.309
Jonathan looked at his mother in horror.

28
00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.732
Had she really just called him "Johnnyboy" in front of this girl?

29
00:01:32.512 --> 00:01:34.634
The beautiful girl flashed him an amused smile.

30
00:01:35.355 --> 00:01:38.677
"Johnnyboy?" "It's Jonathan," he said quickly.

31
00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:39.978
"What's your name?"

32
00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:42.220
"Marissa," she said.

33
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.561
"Nice to meet you."

34
00:01:44.442 --> 00:01:44.902
"Me too.

35
00:01:45.603 --> 00:01:46.264
I mean you too.

36
00:01:47.064 --> 00:01:47.845
I'd better go getting.

37
00:01:48.405 --> 00:01:49.586
I mean, I'd better get going!"

38
00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:53.910
Jonathan ran toward his coach before he could make things even worse.

39
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:59.074
"Ack!" he thought with embarrassment.

40
00:01:59.094 --> 00:02:00.816
"That was so awkward!"

41
00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:04.517
The rest of the team was already huddled around Coach Wattenbarger.

42
00:02:04.537 --> 00:02:07.699
"I'm glad everyone's here today," the coach said.

43
00:02:08.299 --> 00:02:11.560
Though with his brow furrowed as usual, he certainly didn't look glad.

44
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.042
"That means we have two extra players to use as substitutes.

45
00:02:15.682 --> 00:02:18.343
Max will play the entire game because he's the best player in the league.

46
00:02:19.144 --> 00:02:20.264
He'll be our only forward."

47
00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:22.065
Jonathan frowned.

48
00:02:22.845 --> 00:02:24.966
He'd never been on a team that used only one forward.

49
00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:28.188
And he'd never been on a team that hadn't used him as a forward.

50
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.023
He tried to catch Carlos' eye, but Carlos was listening closely to Coach Wattenbarger.

51
00:02:34.484 --> 00:02:37.246
"Make sure to pass the ball to Max," the coach went on.

52
00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:39.027
"What if he's not open?"

53
00:02:39.647 --> 00:02:40.228
Aaron asked.

54
00:02:40.248 --> 00:02:41.849
"I'll be open."

55
00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:43.350
Max sounded smug.

56
00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.712
"Max is the best player in the league," the coach repeated.

57
00:02:47.472 --> 00:02:49.454
Jonathan was starting to get tired of hearing that.

58
00:02:49.474 --> 00:02:53.016
"Carlos, you're playing left midfield," the coach said.

59
00:02:53.777 --> 00:02:54.477
Carlos nodded.

60
00:02:55.078 --> 00:02:56.258
That was his usual position.

61
00:02:56.919 --> 00:02:58.500
"Jonathan Cho: center midfield."

62
00:02:59.224 --> 00:03:01.145
"But I always play forward," Jonathan said.

63
00:03:01.165 --> 00:03:02.786
"No arguing!"

64
00:03:03.206 --> 00:03:03.927
the coach snapped.

65
00:03:04.607 --> 00:03:07.629
He assigned the remaining positions before telling the team to drink some water.

66
00:03:07.649 --> 00:03:11.111
"Then get on the field and win, win, win!"

67
00:03:12.631 --> 00:03:14.993
Jonathan ran back to his parents to get his water bottle.

68
00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.655
Marissa was still there, petting Pastrami.

69
00:03:19.675 --> 00:03:22.297
"How's it going?"

70
00:03:22.637 --> 00:03:23.497
Mrs. Cho asked.

71
00:03:24.118 --> 00:03:24.918
Jonathan groaned.

72
00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:28.340
"This is going to be the worst soccer season ever," he said.

73
00:03:29.172 --> 00:03:31.533
"Our awful coach only cares about his son, Max.

74
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.754
And Max's ego is bigger than a World Cup stadium!"

75
00:03:35.695 --> 00:03:37.375
Marissa gave Jonathan a startled look.

76
00:03:38.056 --> 00:03:39.796
Then she leaped to her feet and hurried away.

77
00:03:42.998 --> 00:03:46.639
Jonathan blinked in surprise as she sat down on a chair near a woman who was talking to

78
00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:47.560
Coach Wattenbarger.

79
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.061
"I think you just insulted Marissa's father and brother, Johnnyboy," Mrs.

80
00:03:52.102 --> 00:03:52.982
Cho said softly.

81
00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.023
Jonathan's dad frowned.

82
00:03:55.043 --> 00:03:57.864
"You need to respect your coach and do what he tells you, Jonathan."

83
00:03:59.268 --> 00:04:00.969
"Sorry," Jonathan mumbled.

84
00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.531
He knew he should apologize to Marissa too.

85
00:04:04.331 --> 00:04:08.193
But he hadn't even been able to tell her his dog's name without stumbling over his words!

86
00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:12.796
Anyway, there was nothing he could do now—the game was about to start.

87
00:04:13.637 --> 00:04:15.318
Jonathan joined his teammates on the field.

88
00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:21.981
They faced the Gray Wolves, who had a much cooler team name than Team Wattenbarger.

89
00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:23.943
The referee blew the whistle.

90
00:04:25.504 --> 00:04:26.044
Game on!

91
00:04:30.556 --> 00:04:33.919
A Gray Wolves player passed the ball to a forward, who dribbled it up the field.

92
00:04:34.679 --> 00:04:36.581
But Carlos blocked him, forcing him to pass.

93
00:04:37.822 --> 00:04:41.004
Aaron intercepted the pass and kicked the ball to his twin, Andrew.

94
00:04:44.447 --> 00:04:47.169
Jonathan raced up the field until he got open in front of Andrew.

95
00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:51.212
"Pass to Max!"

96
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:52.613
their coach yelled.

97
00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:54.675
Andrew passed the ball to Max.

98
00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.222
Max dribbled it toward the goal, but two Gray Wolves players blocked him.

99
00:05:01.243 --> 00:05:03.384
"Shoot the ball, Max!"

100
00:05:04.145 --> 00:05:08.187
Coach Wattenbarger yelled, even though Max was double-teamed and Jonathan was open.

101
00:05:09.168 --> 00:05:13.091
Max took a shot, but a Gray Wolves player intercepted the ball and kicked it hard up the

102
00:05:13.131 --> 00:05:19.055
field. Jonathan ran to the ball and started to dribble.

103
00:05:19.956 --> 00:05:21.517
He raced toward the Gray Wolves goal.

104
00:05:22.618 --> 00:05:25.320
Yes! He was about to score the first goal of the game!

105
00:05:28.932 --> 00:05:30.053
"Pass to Max!"

106
00:05:30.654 --> 00:05:31.454
the coach screamed.

107
00:05:31.474 --> 00:05:33.757
"Cho! Pass to Max!"

108
00:05:34.757 --> 00:05:36.919
Jonathan groaned, but he passed the ball.

109
00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.901
Max shot it toward the goal.

110
00:05:39.662 --> 00:05:41.924
The goalie dived for the ball, but he was too late.

111
00:05:42.865 --> 00:05:44.086
Max scored the first point.

112
00:05:44.827 --> 00:05:49.491
Everyone on Team Wattenbarger cheered, along with the coach and friends and families on the sideline.

113
00:05:56.084 --> 00:05:59.625
Max and Jonathan gave each other high fives as they ran to the middle of the field for

114
00:05:59.645 --> 00:06:00.165
the kickoff.

115
00:06:03.146 --> 00:06:06.747
Jonathan hadn't scored the point, but at least he'd assisted with the first goal.

116
00:06:07.927 --> 00:06:11.888
After the kickoff the Gray Wolves passed the ball from one player to the next until the ball

117
00:06:11.928 --> 00:06:12.648
was near the goal.

118
00:06:13.469 --> 00:06:17.750
But the Wattenbarger defense blocked the ball and got it to Aaron, who was halfway up the field.

119
00:06:20.931 --> 00:06:22.891
A Gray Wolves midfielder ran in front of Aaron.

120
00:06:23.891 --> 00:06:25.812
Fortunately, Jonathan was wide open.

121
00:06:26.832 --> 00:06:30.616
Unfortunately, Coach Wattenbarger yelled, "Pass the ball to Max!"

122
00:06:31.537 --> 00:06:34.599
Max wasn't open, but Aaron kicked the ball toward him anyway.

123
00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:39.044
A Gray Wolves defender intercepted it.

124
00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:44.128
He passed it to a midfielder, who passed it to a forward, who took a great shot.

125
00:06:45.089 --> 00:06:48.733
But the Wattenbarger goalie dived across the goal and made an even greater save.

126
00:06:49.513 --> 00:06:51.976
He kicked the ball down the field, and it soared into the air.

127
00:06:57.716 --> 00:07:00.498
A Wattenbarger defender jumped up and headed the ball to Jonathan.

128
00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:05.261
Jonathan headed the ball a short distance up the field.

129
00:07:07.002 --> 00:07:09.023
Then he ran to it and dribbled toward the goal.

130
00:07:12.485 --> 00:07:15.107
Yes! He'd set up a perfect shot for himself.

131
00:07:15.127 --> 00:07:17.068
"Pass to Max!"

132
00:07:17.668 --> 00:07:18.889
Coach Wattenbarger roared.

133
00:07:19.589 --> 00:07:23.772
Jonathan reluctantly did what he was told, allowing Max to score his second goal.

134
00:07:28.608 --> 00:07:29.869
The whistle blew for halftime.

135
00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:33.551
The score was 2–0, with Team Wattenbarger in the lead.

136
00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:37.433
Jonathan's teammates, including Carlos, chanted, "Max!

137
00:07:37.973 --> 00:07:42.996
Max!" Jonathan bent down and adjusted his shin guards so nobody would notice his silence.

138
00:07:43.876 --> 00:07:45.497
The chanting was loud and annoying.

139
00:07:46.157 --> 00:07:47.378
At least it seemed that way to him.
